atlas surface

architecture page-composition
  source_path deploy/tailwind/styles/page-components.pcss
  source_path deploy/tailwind/styles/reading-surface.pcss
  invariant public agenda, feed, map, media and reading surface styles are compiled assets linked by the shared page renderer
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_events_test.sh checks the native agenda and served component stylesheet
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/native_experience_composition.h
  source_path deploy/tailwind/styles/native-experience.pcss
  source_path site/matrix/native-experience.css
  invariant native experience layout rules are compiled from PostCSS and linked at the compositor head position
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/native_experience_composition_test.c checks the stylesheet link and the absence of inline style emission
  canonical_name PageComposition
  family surface
  domain Surface / Public Page
  layer surface/public
  semantic_question What does a person see on a subject's page or a main public route, given the kinds of material it actually has?
  purpose Lowers a published /w/<slug> page as several reading rhythms people already know instead of one item shape per character. Canonical owner readers and a native port of the census reader normalize stories, video, pictures, recordings and conversation into one stream per kind; a CUE-declared region sequence consumes those streams in order (lead story, Watch shelf, Photos field, Latest index, Listen tracklist, conversation, More list), each region with its own DOM topology and human label, and a region exists only when its material does. Tabs name published ways into the page in ordinary words. The page carries no machine vocabulary; what it cannot be read to imply travels as metadata.
  maturity implemented
  consumes PublicationOccurrence
  consumes InternetSource
  consumes WorldFragment
  consumes HumanCommunityBody
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/front_community.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/front_editorial.h
  invariant an apex front (/, /discover, /today on aurekai.work/.life/.live/.shop) is one composer: edition strip, headline with beat chips, lead, then the dispatch grid (work) or watch/listen/reading/what's-on/pictured regions (others), the standard band, and the page ends; no generic regions, sections or continuation blocks are laid under it
  invariant a source whose twin was read again after its publication_occurrence ledger was last written is read from the retained body, so a stale ledger cannot pin a front to weeks-old items
  forbidden_inference an item on a front -> endorsement, ranking by importance, or that the front holds everything its sources published that day
  invariant public fronts lead to account-scoped applications without displaying an application sample catalogue or a presentation-system showcase
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/work_entrance_test.mjs checks the account application entrance and absence of public demo cards and presentation showcases
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/community_journey.test.mjs verifies a public homepage opens the exact native conversation while personal hosts exclude the shared social entrance
  invariant the public conversation entrance does not set the editorial replacement flag, so an empty or unavailable social selection cannot suppress fallback lead material
  invariant ordinary WebAddress builds use the portable all target; release acceptance is explicit for one selected frozen candidate and never an implicit developer-specific historical directory
  source_path scripts/release/public_surface_rollout.mjs
  source_path scripts/release/tests/public_surface_rollout.test.mjs
  invariant release staging resolves inherited binary links to their existing terminal files, rejects link cycles, and freezes the native Meter executable while connecting an existing configured Meter database to account work
  witness scripts/release/tests/public_surface_rollout.test.mjs checks long inherited link chains, cycle refusal, frozen Meter material and the Meter source selection
  witness scripts/release/tests/public_surface_rollout.test.mjs verifies the frozen Source Desk and source-publication browser dependency closure, refuses missing modules, and binds browser readback to exact release bytes
  invariant release acceptance uses the selected frozen browser and site trees plus the candidate public CMS and Auth executables; activation requires every current acceptance group with matching verifier, static local fixture dependency, environment and browser executable identity
  invariant every browser HTTP fixture reads candidate assets; all frozen modules are compiled to check static imports; companion-only fixture modules are hashed separately from the public HTTP route set
  witness docs/engineering/live-rollout-20261021.md records the 2026-10-23 s6CwWg public activation after 14 acceptance groups and 164 local plus 164 public HTTP readbacks; live authenticated saves remain unverified
  forbidden_inference passing release acceptance -> identity of computed imports, runtime-read fixture data or external package contents outside the declared static closure
  consumes MusicRecording
  consumes MediaProgram
  consumes PresentationTemplate
  publishes ComposedPublicPage
  node_types PageRegion
  node_types PageStream
  node_types PageTab
  edge_types composes
  edge_types lowers
  invariant a region exists only when its material kind is present; a subject with only stories grows no empty Watch, Listen or conversation heading
  invariant regions that share a material stream consume it in declared order, so one story is never shown by two regions of the same page
  invariant the executor branches on region topology and material only; a region role, grammar, source or World name inside it would be a route-local page in disguise (Makefile surface-programs-verify refuses it)
  invariant a World fragment's subject address scheme selects the canonical owner reader (community, recording, program); the page never queries media, music or conversation tables for itself
  invariant one story reached through two carriers is one story, keyed by title or canonical link, and stories across sources are ordered newest first with an unreadable date sorting last rather than being guessed
  invariant visible copy never names the machinery: no World, observed, closure, candidate, grammar, projection, occurrence, character name or subject-address scheme reaches page text; the character is declared in data-character and the cannot-infer statement in a bonfyre:cannot-infer meta element
  invariant every composed public document carries an inert bonfyre-surface-scene.v1 compatibility envelope and stable page/region continuity names derived from that exact server emission; the envelope is a hand-off descriptor, never visible copy or browser-owned material
  invariant PageComposition never mounts SurfaceRuntime: the exact canonical module is projected as a static asset for a future owned ApplicationBinding, while the compatibility document remains complete and readable without a client compositor
  invariant a route with no retained material declines the PageComposition compatibility adapter and falls through to its declared CUE-native surface; an empty compatibility document never displaces an owner-backed native program
  invariant a published addressed World with no declared sources still lowers a complete native empty page; absence of source membership cannot reopen the retired browser renderer
  invariant a grammar with no human label in page-composition.cue is not linked; an internal name is never a navigation word
  invariant tabs are the authored grammar list followed by any other grammar a published fragment opens, so a published way into the page is never reachable only by typing its address
  invariant a relative time ("2h ago") is emitted only inside a public projection that lives at most sixty seconds, so it cannot drift into a false statement
  invariant a subject reference shown to a person is humanized from its handle until a profile owner supplies a display name; the page does not invent a name
  invariant a story's byline is the maker the source names (sub_field, dc:creator, Atom author) when it is short, otherwise the publisher's registrable domain taken from the source URL; a source handle or internet_source label is never shown as a name
  invariant retained bodies are read by the census contract the retired browser reader used: dotted and indexed fields, an empty extract as the body itself, {today-iso}-style date tokens, JSON escapes decoded, feed entities decoded (twice, for feeds that escape twice) before the page escapes again
  invariant a twin with a published content_flag whose review_state is not cleared is withheld from every page until a person clears it, and an item a source marks nsfw, sensitive, over_18 or is_nsfw (on the item, its post or its community) is withheld without judgement
  invariant a video or image source's item joins Watch or Photos only when it carries a picture; the same item without one is a headline, and every other source kind is a story (nativePageSourceKinds)
  invariant a picture reaches the page only as an https URL completed by the source's declared image_base (absolute, @host field, pre|post or origin), rejected if truncated or if it contains a quote, angle bracket, backslash or space, and is written lazy, async, with no referrer and empty alt
  invariant a remote video is linked to where it was published; only a same-origin safe asset plays in place
  invariant a main public route (/discover, /channels, /community, /board, /parcels) is a composed page when page-composition.cue declares a program for it; the program names source families, a source cap and its region sequence, and families fill the cap in declared order a share at a time so every named family contributes
  invariant a program's sources are allocated from the whole admitted source ledger when it is present: the channels that have waited longest for a reader come first, no single publisher may hold more than an eighth of a surface's sources and no single protocol more than a third; each route length is an offset in that complete stable order, never an offset inside an arbitrary query prefix, so an admitted source remains reachable through the route's bounded continuation; where the ledger is absent or thin the declared families still fill the page, so a page is never emptier for the ledger existing
  invariant a program's source window is no larger than the number of sources its declared rhythms visibly carry, so a continuation never advances past a selected publisher that a reader did not meet
  invariant a source whose current retained body no longer lowers still contributes the fields the item archive retained; the archive is a record of what this estate read, not a claim that the source still publishes it or a substitute for richer current source media
  invariant a placed thing carries what else this estate holds around it: every placed material (an organizer's GEO, a photograph's own point, a place's coordinates, a wildlife record) within a short walk, nearest first, with the distance measured between the two stated points and said in a person's words; being near something is never shown as being about it
  invariant every response leaves through one boundary that compresses it: a body a caller can read as gzip is gzipped (nothing already packed, nothing under 1.4 KB), the answer says it varies by what the caller reads, and a caller that does not read gzip receives exactly the bytes the page composed
  invariant what may be packed is decided by the answer's own headers, never by its body: a track list whose files live under /audio/ on their host, or a gallery naming image paths, is a page and is compressed like one
  invariant a composed page is kept and served again for a bounded moment: only where it is nobody's in particular (no query, no signed-in reader), keyed by the state of the material it was composed from and by the clock at ten-minute granularity, which is finer than the coarsest thing a page says about time
  invariant the estate warms its own pages rather than charging the first visitor for them: the warmer composes each public route exactly as a request would, reads no source, admits nothing, and can only fill what a request would have composed anyway
  invariant publication may explicitly defer an external reheat batch and compose the complete retained generation already held; deferral is recorded as such and is never represented as a fresh source observation
  invariant a page carries an ETag over exactly the bytes it composed, and a caller that already holds them is answered 304 with no body; a private answer keeps its private cache directive in that answer
  invariant the commons that keep this estate's pictures are named in the head as preconnect and dns-prefetch, from the declared picture-origin table, so a browser opens those connections while it reads rather than when it meets the first picture; nothing is fetched there and no other host is named
  invariant a time is computed, not switched: reading a calendar entry's moment uses arithmetic for UTC and sets the host's zone only when the zone actually changes, because reloading a timezone database twice per entry cost a page more than everything else it did
  invariant `page-contributions` composes every declared route exactly as the server does and reports what each route would show now, by source; it renders to nobody and measures this estate's surfaces, never a reader
  invariant the static export follows a public program's own next link until that program ends, bounded by the same four-hundred-length route guard as the server; an arbitrary exporter page cap cannot turn an admitted source into an uncirculated one
  invariant a retained-item export is a finite closure: every selected item page must materialize with a 200 body or the generation refuses. A partial archive is never an activatable public release.
  invariant the static export also carries the admitted SourceDepth index and every admitted source profile under exact query-coordinate object keys, so the public source lattice does not disappear when its dynamic origin is absent
  invariant a family a program does not name never reaches its page; selection is by authored family, never by a title, a URL domain or a source's own claims
  invariant an addressed World page uses nativePageWorldRegions; the topics rhythm belongs to main routes and would otherwise take the stories More keeps
  invariant a front page's phase is derived from this estate's own clock (nativeHomePhases: the hour each begins, in BONFYRE_LOCAL_ZONE): the phase renames the page and reorders the routes below it, and can admit no material, no source and no route the territory does not already publish; every visitor at the same hour sees the same arrangement, so it is derived composition and never personalization
  invariant each territory apex (aurekai.live, .life, .shop, .work and their www. hosts, port ignored) opens on its own composed front page (Right now, Today, Just released, Work) ahead of any SitePresentation naming that apex; institution and subdomain hosts are not territory apexes and keep their own homes, and a machine request to the apex keeps its machine answer
  invariant each territory apex has an offline SubjectFabric reader closure over admitted SourceFrontier census sources, and its routes select only explicit estate-owned SourceCollections whose declared family or carried material matches the CUE route; a request consumes the compiled route material and editorial contract and never reopens retained bodies to rediscover global membership
  invariant one compiled public route page keeps one resolved host subject and one read-only SubjectFabric connection across route material, region order, editorial contract, compatibility source selection, and every preview section; a section cannot silently resolve a different subject or reopen a different projection generation within that page
  forbidden_inference reusing one read connection across page sections -> authority to union subjects, widen a SourceCollection, admit an unselected item, or treat the cached projection as current after a later rebuild
  invariant a SubjectFabric route cut retains an atomic build manifest over the exact admitted-reader, Scene-query, published-SourceCollection, item-stream, page-composition and surface-program inputs it read; its route digest includes the rendered contract and every normalized renderer-visible item field, and a failed replacement rolls back the entire route-table reset
  invariant normalized item payload is stored once per source/item/material coordinate and explicit subject membership remains independent; the subject_material compatibility view reconstructs the prior reader shape for WebAddress without making shared bytes evidence of shared subject identity or authority
  invariant an item page opened from a compiled public route reads that route's selected normalized material through the exact host subject and route membership relation; once a verified route cut exists for that host, an unselected item cannot reopen through a legacy source body
  invariant a signed-in Save of a compiled item takes the same exact host-subject route membership and normalized material as its item page before any native saved_item write, including repeat Save; an item selected for a different subject or omitted from this route cannot pass through a legacy feed fallback
  invariant when a later compiled cut omits an item, the public item page and feed omit it and new Save writes are refused; the actor who had already saved it may still read their own private snapshot until they unsave, after which that page is refused for them too
  invariant a territory with a committed subject-route cut publishes its Atom feed from that same host-subject route-item membership and normalized material, never from all same-family retained sources; its item links return to native pages on that host, its ETag is stable until the cut changes, and another territory cannot inherit its entries
  invariant the committed subject-route cut is verified by the Bun SQLite and SHA-256 owner in the live automation path; it recomputes the exact bounded input frontier and all projection-table row digests before a route cut is trusted
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/subject_projection_precompute_test.sh compares Bun and legacy verifier answers byte-for-byte on a committed fixture and refuses changed item material or tampered projection rows; cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh uses the Bun verifier before exercising its public route
  invariant the Atom feed is a separate read-only native module; AddressPlane resolves the host before invocation, and bounded XML assembly either emits a complete response or refuses it. A declared WebSub hub must be a safe HTTPS address, never an arbitrary header value
  invariant a static release that carries a page advertising /feed.atom must carry the same host-scoped Atom response as a file or refuse the release; the exporter cannot reselect feed entries from another source catalogue
  invariant the standing route rebuild reads a completed census item generation and a SubjectFabric closure from the same automation run; a failed item export leaves the previous complete item file intact and refuses the dependent route rebuild
  invariant a front page names its place (Aurekai) instead of pointing back to it and offers the other territories as Live, Life, Shop and Work
  invariant every retained item has a stable page key (a digest of its source and its link, or title) and opens /o/<source>/<key>; no composed page writes an anchor without an href, and an item with neither a page nor a public link is text
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh opens a compiled exact SourceCollection route and selected item, signs in two people, writes one native saved_item from normalized material, keeps it private, and refuses an excluded same-family source, a cross-territory repeat Save, and a foreign Origin
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh starts from retained source bodies and receipt paths, runs the native census exporter, proves a reference-candidate Ghost profile dresses only the selected route material, discovers a host-scoped Atom feed from that page, receives a stable ETag/304, and sees the excluded source and other territory stay outside the feed
  witness 2026-09-30 cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh, page_composition_test.sh, and page_programs_test.sh pass after request-scoped SubjectFabric reuse; they prove rendered route behavior, not a measured live latency improvement
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/atom_feed_test.c exercises compiled subject isolation, XML escaping, HEAD, ETag/304, invalid hub refusal, and guest-readable CMS fallback without another Python test program
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/a2a_surface_test.sh proves four territory roots emit distinct server-side titles, self-canonical addresses and a working public-search form from the generated home template, including when CMS is unavailable
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh proves a published World with no admitted sources answers a plain native empty page without visible machine vocabulary or browser composition
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh recompiles after the selected item leaves the census stream, proving the public feed and page withdraw it, a different actor cannot save or read it, the original saver can still read the private snapshot, and unsaving removes that last private reading
  witness scripts/tests/export_static_estate_depth_test.sh proves the route walk carries its advertised native Atom feed into the static tree while retaining pagination through the thirteenth Discover length
  invariant an item page's verbs are links or forms that work without a script: play in place (PeerTube embed from the video's own host), view the picture full size, open the place in a map, read or watch at the publisher, share by mail with the page's own address, sign in to save and return, and more from the maker narrowed by ?from=
  invariant each main route has its own rhythm and its own families: Discover a mixed feed, Watch a video grid, Channels two panes selected by ?s=, Community groups by who is posting, Boards a picture wall, Map a plate beside its numbered list, Releases and Advisories a ledger, Research an index, Search typed results; no two routes share a family, so a person does not meet the same sources on every page
  invariant a front page is sections into those routes, each previewed in that route's own rhythm with its words as the heading and a See all way in, not one more feed
  invariant ?from= narrows a page to one maker or publisher and ?q= to matching text; both are shown as plain words with a Show all link, and neither selects sources outside the route's families
  invariant sources fill a page by fair share (the stream cap divided across its sources) so the first few sources cannot crowd out the rest
  invariant search is a GET form in every composed page's header and answers from the retained text of the page programs' families
  invariant a property is a continuous subject at /s/parcel/<account>: every open reads the observed Tarrant roll for its facts and its same-street neighbours, offers the parcel aperture's own verbs in plain words (See this market; with write scope Watch this property, Open an opportunity), and falls back to the legacy subject door for an account the roll does not hold and for machine requests
  invariant search that reads like an address or an account also searches the observed property roll and lists matches before retained material, each opening its property page
  invariant a lead needs a date or a picture; an undated, pictureless item never leads a page
  invariant topics group public threads by where they are happening (the publisher), newest first within each, keeping the first-appearance order of places
  invariant a place is plotted only from GeoJSON geometry, Darwin Core decimal coordinates or plain latitude/longitude pairs inside the globe; 0,0 is unknown, not a place; points sit on a Natural Earth land mask with no tile provider and no implied precision
  invariant a publisher relay host (hn.algolia.com, feeds.bbci.co.uk, api.wikimedia.org, ...) is named for its publisher only through the authored host table; the table replaces a byline and never selects material
  invariant a native surface document loads /assets/aurekai-native.css and titles itself with the grammar's human label, so no native route renders as unstyled markup or a program name
  invariant the fallback home template carries generated slots for server-resolved identity and authored navigation, the public search form, and the existing home-weather fragment as authored markup; a request does not scan/copy the whole template to splice search, rewrite territory copy, or fetch public weather through a browser compositor, and missing CMS copy stays a generic server-owned floor
  invariant published territory-home copy is located against one immutable template and assembled in one allocation; a missing region leaves the original document untouched, and a territory class cannot inject HTML attributes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/territory_home_test.c proves four published territory presentations, absent-CMS fallback, and atomic refusal of an incomplete template or unsafe territory class
  forbidden_inference a composed page -> an editorial judgement, endorsement or ranking of importance; newest-first is a date order and the lead is simply the newest story
  forbidden_inference a picture shown from a source -> a licence to republish it, a copy held by this estate, or a claim about who is depicted
  forbidden_inference an item not withheld -> screened and cleared material; most retained bodies are never looked at by a screen that could see anything
  forbidden_inference a Watch or Listen region -> rights to show the media, a playback session or a viewer identity
  forbidden_inference a conversation region -> federation, moderation beyond the owner's accepted state, or membership of the reader
  forbidden_inference a human label such as Schedule or Map -> the grammar behind it being fully built; the tab links whatever the published route already serves
  forbidden_inference the absence of machine vocabulary on the page -> the absence of the boundaries it used to state; they moved to metadata and to the machine carriers (manifest, feed, outbox, events)
  forbidden_inference a source filed under gaming or vulnerabilities -> every item it carries being a release or advisory; source family is acquisition/routing evidence and high-claim routes require their own compiled source/form contract
  forbidden_inference a matching subject-projection input or route digest -> source truth, current provider availability, rights, authority, endorsement, or a fresh external observation
  known_gap /listings still lowers a donor slot document over an empty offer owner; it is not in the composed pages' nav and remains reachable as a system disclaimer
  known_gap the retired territory home's intake form (bring in a public address) and external-estate search are no longer on the apex front pages; they remain at /_surface/intake and /_surface/external-estate without a human entry point
  known_gap native operator documents (/inbox, /territory, /packs, /link, /console, /studio) are now readable but their slot copy still states capability and authority terms rather than what a person can do
  known_gap the map plate draws 50 points and the first placed family fills it, so on /parcels earthquakes crowd out species sightings and bike networks
  known_gap item pages outside a compiled route still use the legacy retained-body and item-archive readers; a compiled route keeps only its selected normalized material, not every version or every item ever observed
  known_gap Pass 1 is partial: PageComposition now emits a SurfaceScene-compatible, server-side hand-off but remains the retained-material adapter until SitePresentation/ApplicationBinding/ExperienceStage declarations own each route; no legacy public route mounts SurfaceRuntime yet
  known_gap the composed /stage route now draws only the events family, but it still reads retained event items rather than a dedicated Event owner projection carrying parsed lifecycle/time/place fields. Place remains unregistered (spatial_observation is empty). Observed marketplace material is owned as service_offer and /market reads it, but Listings has not yet projected that owner kind and remains a donor page over an empty owner
  known_gap a property page performs two scans of the columnar roll (about 3.5 s on the estate) and address search one (about 2.5 s); neither is indexed or cached yet
  known_gap properties carry no coordinates in the roll, so a property page has no map and the Map route does not show properties
  known_gap some PeerTube instances (tube.tchncs.de) put an anti-bot challenge in front of their embed, and the Art Institute IIIF host refuses non-browser clients; neither was observable as a person would see it from the estate or a headless browser
  known_gap a story still links out to its publisher; a subject whose story should open inside Aurekai (an event, a property, a venue) needs its own addressed page before a lead can stay in place
  known_gap video titles are humanized from the program's subject reference because MediaProgram carries no title; a subject-owner title join is not built
  known_gap a non-date meta field (views, magnitude, stars) is read and not shown, so The ground moved lists places without magnitudes; the census row does not say what unit a meta value is in
  known_gap the Art Institute IIIF host answers 403 to every non-browser client, so whether those pictures paint for people was not observable from the estate or a headless browser
  known_gap the published night_subject rows (venues, a showcase, egress) are synthetic demo-grid subjects and are deliberately not composed into the real-city Tonight page; that page is still fed by the news sources its World names
  known_gap the /w catalogue is a native surface program whose masthead still prints the program name; its copy is not yet under this vocabulary law
  known_gap an Event source-observation stream exists as publication_occurrence, but its parsed Event projection is not yet a page-program input; Place has no admitted spatial owner stream. /stage is now an events-only CUE page program, while Map remains reached through its donor surface. The observed marketplace chain is owner-backed at /market, but has not yet become the Listings page program
  known_gap Releases and Advisories now exclude weak source-family matches through conservative publisher/form contracts. They are not yet a full owner-backed multi-facet ItemMaterialClassification projection, so a newly trustworthy publisher still needs an authored contract before its otherwise relevant material can appear there.
