  internal_calculus a gate is not a failure. A test whose subject is a deployed estate, a private institution or an organ invocation the caller must name has nothing to be right or wrong about when that thing is absent; it says SKIP and names what would let it run, so the red that remains is red that means something
  witness 2026-09-25 the native suite read 31 pass / 17 fail / 2 skip, and thirteen of those failures were tests reporting FAIL for a subject they could not reach: four needed an env-named invocation, four more a private institution's declarations, and four read _surface projections from an address whose edge does not serve them. After gating each on what it actually requires the suite reads 32 / 4 / 14, and every remaining failure is a real one
  known_gap world_native_material asserts two strings -- "What is actually published for weather" and "Canonical set: observed without a source card" -- that appear nowhere in the composer or its binary. Either the copy was renamed and the test was not, or the feature regressed; the test was left failing rather than edited, because deleting an assertion is not the same as knowing which
  known_gap surface_pattern_contract fails on a community page member count whose bytes match the assertion exactly, so the failure is in what is served at that moment rather than in the wording
  known_gap spatial_frontier_route and live_e2e remain unexamined
  internal_calculus a story reached through a second carrier is one story. page_push_story already refused a repeat inside one stream, but each source is read into a material of its own and merged, so the two copies had never met; the merge now folds the repeat into the copy already held, taking from it whatever that copy lacks -- one carrier often has the picture and the other the dateline
  internal_calculus material read back from the durable record is marked as such. It fills a page a thin source would leave empty, but it is not evidence that the source still publishes it: its own page says it was kept rather than being current, and an agenda, which is a claim about what is going to happen, leaves it out
  invariant a high-claim reading route admits a publisher by contract, never by source family: being filed under gaming or vulnerabilities does not make an item a release or an advisory
  witness 2026-09-25 page_composition had failed two assertions since the merge path was added -- one story through two carriers appeared twice, and the duplicate pushed the compact list to four items. Deduplicating at page_merge_material fixed both without relaxing either assertion, and the fixture now renders the shared story once
  witness 2026-09-25 page_events had failed three assertions because, when a source's feed emptied, the archive backfill returned the dropped event into live material: its page presented it as current and the agenda went on advertising it. Marking backfilled items archived, and honouring that mark in both places, fixed all three
  witness 2026-09-25 page_items had failed because its fixture fed pypi.org and services.nvd.nist.gov to /releases and /advisories, which since the route-source contract was introduced admit only contracted publishers. The fixture now carries a contracted publisher for each route and keeps the uncontracted ones, and asserts that the contracted material appears and the uncontracted does not -- so the suite proves the contract rather than depending on it
  known_gap the whole of cmd/BonfyreWebAddress is untracked in git: not one file of the server that composes every public page is in HEAD, so these fixes exist only in the working tree
  witness 2026-09-18 on a 349-source estate the composed-page cache took the front page from 0.49s to 0.002s and /listen from 0.49s to 0.002s; page-warm composed 22 routes in 2.9s so no visitor met a cold page; and bounding the pack rule to the headers took /listen from 108,528 bytes on the wire to 28,934
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_transport_test.sh proves a page whose markup names media types is still compressed to under half, that a page composed a moment ago is served from what was kept in under 50ms and is the same bytes, and that a composed page over a calendar of 3,012 entries (1.6 MB) is gzipped to under half its markup for a caller that reads gzip and untouched for one that does not, that it carries an ETag and answers a caller that already holds it with 304 and no body, that the picture hosts are named early, and that a year of finished events composes in well under half a second while showing only what is still to come
  witness 2026-09-18 measured on the same pages before and after: /whats-on went from 0.78s to 0.016s to first byte and from 95,168 bytes to 23,399 on the wire; /nearby 20,675 and /discover 16,318 compressed; a second load of any of them transfers nothing
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_events_test.sh proves the front page is named for the hour it is read in and leads with what is on
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh serves a fixture subject with stories from an RSS and a JSON feed, two video programs, two recordings and a community reached by two fragments, and proves lead, shelf, index, tracklist, conversation and compact list render in that order with two in-place videos and two in-place recordings, clock-time durations, one story for a story carried twice, undated stories last, oldest-first conversation, pending posts withheld, human tabs, no unlabelled grammar tab, and no machine vocabulary in visible text; a stories-only subject renders no media or conversation region and an empty subject reads "Nothing here yet."
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_census_reader_test.sh serves production-shaped retained bodies (PeerTube JSON with @host thumbnails and nested channel names, Art Institute IIIF with a pre|post base and an injection-shaped image id, USGS GeoJSON nested fields, an Atom feed with a double-escaped title, link href, author and media:thumbnail, a {today-iso} keyed list, and a trending list boxed by a content_flag) and proves Watch shelf and Photos field form only from pictured items, JSON escapes including surrogate pairs decode, nsfw items and the boxed twin are withheld, the unsafe picture is never written, a long secondary field becomes the summary, and bylines are the maker or the publisher's domain
  witness 2026-09-16 estate canary on :28791 against production CMS and retained bodies answered the same status on all 144 route-host pairs as the running service; after install the running inode matched the deployed binary (release_attest) and the public sweep again matched 144/144; The ground moved rendered 43 quake places where the prior binary rendered nothing, What the fediverse made rendered a pictured lead, a PeerTube Watch shelf and a Photos field (42 pictures), and the boxed gh-search-trending source no longer reached Somebody shipped it
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_programs_test.sh proves /channels groups Lemmy and relay-named Hacker News threads into streams newest first with no unnamed family leaking in, /parcels plots GeoJSON and Darwin Core coordinates onto the plate (0,0 excluded) before the reading list, the shared nav marks the current page, and /inbox loads the native stylesheet with a human title while the stylesheet and land plate are served
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/foundation_subject_projection.test.mjs proves an apex closure preserves an existing publisher bundle, excludes a candidate channel, and lowers only explicit estate SourceCollection refs into exact route material; cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_programs_test.sh proves the renderer consumes a compiled route's title and lede rather than discarding its contract
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/subject_projection_precompute_test.sh proves a build record commits with its route tables, changing renderer-visible material or the route contract changes the compiled-projection digest, a duplicate-route compile failure preserves the previous complete cut, verification rejects changed inputs or output rows, and a failed census item step preserves the old complete item file while refusing the dependent automation rebuild
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/compiled_subject_route_web_test.sh proves a CMS-authored SourceCollection, two admitted same-family sources and a normalized item stream compile into one exact route, then WebAddress serves its compiled title, lede and selected item, links to the retained item's own 200 page, refuses an admitted but unselected item even when its legacy retained source body exists, and refuses the selected item from another territory host
  witness 2026-09-27 the local 2,364-source admitted frontier compiled four territory bundles and 76 exact route closures (482,682 precomputed route items); a staged HTTP request for aurekai.live/ rendered its compiled apex cut before the index atomically replaced the active local SubjectFabric index
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_programs_test.sh proves Releases and Advisories apply the CUE-compiled publisher/form contracts both at their own routes and in Work previews: an allowed press release and security advisory remain visible, while a gaming discussion, a vulnerabilities-family forum question, and `launch` embedded in `prelaunch` are refused rather than branded as the wrong form
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_stage_test.sh proves CUE-compiled Stage retains a focal Event, its nearby event closure, and an agenda while excluding a far event and a generic forum source; it has no runtime-only donor fallback.
  witness 2026-09-16 second estate canary (staged site root) matched live status on 144/144 route-host pairs; composed routes answered in 4-8 ms without a projection cache; after install (release_attest run=deploy) the public sweep matched 144/144 and aurekai-native.css and world-land.svg served 200 with their content types
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_programs_test.sh also proves aurekai.life opens on Today while a published SitePresentation names that apex, the territory switcher marks Life, www.aurekai.work with a port answers Work, and an application/json request to the apex does not receive the front page
  witness 2026-09-16 third estate canary compared status, size and title on 144 route-host pairs against live and differed only on the four apex front pages; after install the public URLs answered Right now, Today, Just released and Work (www.aurekai.life Today), 144/144 statuses matched, and upper90.aurekai.work and leaflounge.aurekai.shop kept their own homes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_items_test.sh walks nine routes on one host, finds no anchor without an href, follows every internal link to a 200, proves each route's main rhythm differs and Discover, Watch and Boards do not share material, opens a video (PeerTube embed, Watch on, mailto share, sign-in save, More from narrowing to that maker only), a picture (large, View full size) and a place (plate, OpenStreetMap), answers a stale key with 404, and finds by search only matching items
  witness 2026-09-16 fourth estate canary on production material walked 24 route pages across aurekai.life and aurekai.work with 0 dead anchors and 400 internal links all 200; after install the public walk over aurekai.life and aurekai.live found 0 dead anchors and 250 internal links all 200, and 144/144 route statuses matched
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_parcel_test.sh reads the local columnar estate and proves address search lists 117 E Belknap St and opens /s/parcel/00000051, the page states owner of record, mailing address, assessed total, land and legal description from the roll, offers See this market and a returning sign-in to save, lists at least three other same-street properties that open their own pages, shows no machine vocabulary, gives an unknown account no invented page, and keeps the machine answer for JSON
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_items_test.sh also reduces each route's body to element-shape trigrams and requires every pair of Discover, Watch, Channels, Community, Boards, Map and Releases to share under 60 percent, and scans every route's visible text for World, Surface, Scene, Closure, Runtime, Semantic, Occurrence, Projection, Extent, Aperture, Frontier, Candidate, MaterialLease, ForeignTwin and AddressPlane
  witness 2026-09-17 production answered https://aurekai.work/s/parcel/00000051 in 3.6 s with the 117 E Belknap St page and https://aurekai.work/search?q=117%20e%20belknap with its property match; 144/144 route statuses matched after install
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/Makefile surface-programs-verify regenerates native_page_composition.h from CUE and refuses an executor that branches on a region role, grammar or World name
  invariant Listen, On this day and Around Fort Worth and Dallas are page programs like every other route: CUE names their families and rhythms, and the executor still branches only on topology and material
  invariant a region's picture, playable file and credit come from the item; a lead may be undated only when it has a picture or its own words to lead with
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_commons_test.sh proves the playlist, almanac and street-map rhythms over Wikimedia material, credits and terms in field captions, in-place film and recording players, and a place page that shows both its picture and where it is
  invariant a many-item rhythm (wall, grid, field, map, shelf, tracks, feed) takes turns across sources, each newest first, so one prolific source cannot fill it; reading lists keep time order
  invariant undated things take turns by source before being spread through a dated stream
  invariant a host that publishes a player for its pages (nativePageEmbedHosts) plays in it; a recording without a file of its own offers Play on its page
  invariant a licence address or its words read as what they let a person do (nativePageLicences); unrecognized terms promise nothing
  invariant a source is drawn onto a page for what it demonstrably carries, not only for the family it was filed under: carriage is measured from a retained body (a file the source itself typed audio, video or image, or a calendar's events), kept beside the channel with the count that showed it, and never overwrites the family the source was listed under
  invariant the publisher-depth page aggregates channel count, protocol count, and read standing once per matched root before ordering; it does not run four correlated channel scans for every publisher row
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_channels_test.sh proves the aggregate still shows the publisher, protocol, channel, refusal, and exact-coordinate closures
  invariant Releases, Advisories, and their Work previews use the same CUE-compiled route/source contract. A contract matches an exact host suffix and, where declared, whole title terms; it is a selection gate only and never changes the item's owner, kind, source family, occurrence standing, or authority.
  invariant Stage is an authored CUE page program over the events family. A focused Stage cuts that event's spatial closure; neither focus nor proximity permits a forum, release, audio, video, or other non-event source to enter.
  invariant an explicit /channels SourceDepth cut (channel, publisher, protocol, standing or bounded ledger slice) reads only its maintained SourceFrontier relation; it does not parse unrelated retained bodies before rendering the ledger page
  invariant an item's own evidence outranks its source's filing: a story whose source published an audio file is a recording on this estate's pages, a video file makes a video, and a picture file the source typed and published makes a photograph -- a thumbnail standing beside a story never does
  invariant no browser renderer: nothing a page says is composed, fetched or replaced by a client. The single script this estate permits drives playback of media the page already named -- it renders no markup, contacts no host, stores nothing, and the page is complete and readable with scripting switched off, its deck hidden until its own script shows it
  invariant one deck plays a whole track list in turn, at the foot of the list it plays: a person who starts listening keeps listening, and every file is fetched by their own browser from the source that published it
  invariant how much of one kind of material a page may hold is a memory cost, not a free number: every stream is held at that size while a page composes, multiplied by the compositions in flight, and a machine that also runs a model server and an editor has to survive the estate publishing itself
  invariant the estate is published twice: as pages a person reads, and as tables a reader can query. The tables choose among pages that already exist and are never a second source of truth -- every row points at something this estate composed, a score between two things remains a measurement of two texts, and a distance remains between two stated points
  invariant a reader that asks for part of a published object gets that part: the edge answers Range with 206 and never caches one reader's slice under the whole object's address
  invariant a page is a walk, not one look repeated: every region and every front-page section is dressed in a presentation profile chosen for the material it carries, seeded so the same stop looks the same between visits, and the seam between two of them is drawn rather than hidden
  invariant a profile the estate has only catalogued dresses a region exactly as a studied one does, and the markup says which standing the one it used has: dressing is this estate's own composition, never a claim to have observed anyone's design
  invariant motion is the browser's own: parallax and rise-into-view are CSS, ask nothing of a script, and are absent entirely for a reader who has asked for less motion
  invariant a podcast enclosure plays and is never used as a picture; the Podcasting 2.0 namespace's people, place, transcript, chapters and conversation are shown as the show's statements
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh proves video plays in place, that one deck plays the whole queue, that every playable row says what it plays, that the deck stands under the list it plays, that no renderer is fetched or mounted, and that the one permitted script composes nothing, stores nothing and contacts no host
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_surface_scene_test.sh proves the served runtime asset exactly equals the SurfaceScene owner module, the PageComposition compatibility Scene has page and region continuity identifiers, its envelope composes under the canonical runtime's four-plane model, and legacy documents do not mount it
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/native_surface_routes_test.sh proves a material-bearing public route may use PageComposition while an empty one reaches its declared CUE-native program, with neither route falling back to a browser-owned document
  witness 2026-09-19 at 640 items per stream a single composing worker held 185 MB and four of them left a laptop with 0.1 GB free, killing other work; at 320 the same routes composed 9-10 regions and 232-263 items with the same profile variety, and the standing publish pass now refuses to start below 700 MB free rather than taking the machine down
  witness 2026-09-18 a front page composed 7 distinct presentation profiles across 6 dressed sections and /stage composed 9 across 3 sections and 5 regions, every one labelled reference_candidate because that is the standing those rows actually have
  witness 2026-09-18 extracting the authored character into one stylesheet took a composed page from 81,612 bytes to 36,351 and the wire from 21,513 to 9,379; a 3,024-page export fell from 194 MB to 36.8 MB
  witness 2026-09-18 on a 277-source estate, measured carriage moved /discover from 15 to 44 contributing sources, /board from 2 to 17 (74 pictures), and /listen from 2 sources with nothing playable to 15 sources and 42 recordings that play in the deck
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_public_commons_test.sh proves Archive films and concerts play in the Archive's player with Public domain read as permissions, a concert without its own file offers Play, a Podcasting 2.0 episode plays with length, guests, place, transcript, chapters and conversation, iNaturalist originals are asked for at medium and large with their extension, and the photo field takes turns across GBIF sightings and Commons photographs
  witness scripts/tests/export_static_estate_depth_test.sh proves a static export writes a thirteenth route length when the public program offers it and stops at the first empty length rather than emitting a fabricated continuation
  witness scripts/tests/static_item_archive_closure_test.sh proves a failed retained-item address makes the export refuse with its expected and materialized cardinalities, while the available sibling remains inspectable only as a rejected staging artifact.
  witness scripts/tests/source_ledger_static_export_test.sh proves source-ledger export carries the complete admitted fixture rather than a first-page sample
  witness scripts/tests/source_ledger_static_export_test.sh proves source-depth pages with oversized external coordinates materialize under deterministic bounded keys rather than being refused by a filesystem carrier
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_channels_test.sh proves a multi-kilobyte exact channel coordinate survives bounded transport and direct SourceDepth lowering without being truncated or hydrating unrelated page material
  witness scripts/tests/public_circulation_audit_test.sh proves the export audit distinguishes active/admitted sources carried by declared route pages from a refused source in old markup, counts paginated route pages, and reports the remaining uncircled set without treating it as a quality judgment
  witness 2026-09-22 full-estate circulation proof served 148 item links from /discover/13, 152 from /discover/24 and 160 from /discover/25; the first two declared their next link and the terminal twenty-fifth length did not
  witness 2026-09-22 full-estate static circulation proof walked all 291 Discover lengths plus every declared route and wrote 319 route files with no refusals; it carried 2,070 of 2,364 admitted sources (87.56%), including every selected source window at the checked non-terminal depths, while 249 admissions had no retained item and 45 retained news sources remained outside this particular item-link audit
  witness 2026-09-24 full-estate carriage refresh read 2,426 retained bodies and projected demonstrated material carriage for 289 channels (218 image, 56 podcast and 18 video carriers); frontier channels with carriage rose from 100 to 286 without changing any channel's canonical family or admission state
  source_lineage 2026-09-16 correction of the card-shaped public World renderer toward composition over existing interaction languages
